<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>NASA 每日一天文圖 (成大物理分站)</title><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/archivepix.html</link><atom:link href="http://rss.owo.nz/nasa/apod-ncku" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"></atom:link><description>NASA 每日一天文圖 (成大物理分站) - Powered by RSSHub</description><generator>RSSHub</generator><webMaster>contact@rsshub.app (RSSHub)</webMaster><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 01 Aug 2025 00:35:15 GMT</lastBuildDate><ttl>5</ttl><item><title>Supernova 2025rbs in NGC 7331</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/2025rbsAnnotated1024.png&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;星系NGC 7331裡的超新星2025rbs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;影像提供: &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/physics/research/astro/people/bengodson/&quot;&gt;Ben Godson&lt;/a&gt;
(University of Warwick)

 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: A long time ago in a galaxy 50 million light-years away, a star exploded . Light from that supernova was first detected by telescopes on planet Earth on July 14th though, and the extragalactic transient is now known to astronomers as supernova 2025rbs . Presently the brightest supernova in planet Earth&#39;s sky, 2025rbs is a Type Ia supernova, likely caused by the thermonuclear detonation of a white dwarf star that accreted material from a companion in a binary star system. Type Ia supernovae are used as standard candles to establish the distance scale of the universe. The host galaxy of 2025rbs is NGC 7331. Itself a bright spiral galaxy in the northern constellation Pegasus, NGC 7331 is often touted as an analog to our own Milky Way.
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 

很久很久以前，在離地球5000萬光年遠的星系裡，一顆&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/resource/type-ia-supernova/&quot;&gt;恆星發生爆炸&lt;/a&gt;。

不過直到今年的7月14日，地球上的望遠鏡才偵測到來自這例&lt;a href=&quot;https://goto-observatory.org/bright-supernova-2025rbs-discovered-by-goto/&quot;&gt;超新星的光&lt;/a&gt;，天文學家並將這例河外瞬變事件命名為&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wis-tns.org/object/2025rbs&quot;&gt;超新星2025rbs&lt;/a&gt;。

目前是地球天空最明亮&lt;a href=&quot;https://rochesterastronomy.org/supernova.html&quot;&gt;超新星&lt;/a&gt;的2025rbs，其分類為Ia型超新星，因為它可能是雙星系統中的白矮星，吸積伴星的物質後所產生的熱核爆炸。

而&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/mission/roman-space-telescope/type-ia-supernovae/&quot;&gt;Ia型超新星&lt;/a&gt;則可作為標準燭光，用以測定宇宙的距離。

位於北天飛馬座方向、作為2025rbs寄主星系的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap220922.html&quot;&gt;NGC 7331&lt;/a&gt;，本身是一個明亮的螺旋星系，其外觀咸認和我們的銀河系非常類似。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250731.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250731.html</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Coronal Loops on the Sun</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/SunLoops_Vanoni_960.jpg&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;太陽的日冕環&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 影像提供與版權： &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/astro.vano/&quot;&gt;Andrea Vanoni&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Our Sun frequently erupts in loops. Hot solar plasma jumps off the Sun&#39;s surface into prominences , with the most common type of prominence being a simple loop. The loop shape originates from the Sun&#39;s magnetic field , which is traced by spiraling electrons and protons. Many loops into the Sun&#39;s lower corona are large enough to envelop the Earth and are stable enough to last days. They commonly occur near active regions that also include dark sunspots . The featured panel shows four loops, each of which was captured near the Sun &#39;s edge during 2024 and 2025. The images were taken by a small telescope in Mantova , Italy and in a very specific color of light emitted primarily by hydrogen . Some solar prominences suddenly break open and eject particles into the Solar System , setting up a space weather sequence that can affect the skies and wires of Earth. Jigsaw Universe: Astronomy Puzzle of the Day
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 

我們的太陽常發生環狀的爆發。

造成炙熱的太陽&lt;a href=&quot;https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14299&quot;&gt;電漿&lt;/a&gt;從其表面噴出，形成我們稱為&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap240615.html&quot;&gt;日珥&lt;/a&gt;的結構，其中最常見的類型為單環日珥。

這些&lt;a href=&quot;https://daily.wordreference.com/2016/09/30/word-of-the-day-loop/&quot;&gt;環形結構&lt;/a&gt;源自太陽的&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nasa.gov/science-research/heliophysics/nasa-understanding-the-magnetic-sun/&quot;&gt;磁場&lt;/a&gt;，其輪廓由沿磁力線做螺旋運動的電子與質子交織而成。

許多日珥下層的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap240402.html&quot;&gt;日冕&lt;/a&gt;環，大小足以&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap140304.html&quot;&gt;包覆&lt;/a&gt;整個地球，而且可穩定存續數天。

日冕環通常出現在&lt;a href=&quot;https://spaceplace.nasa.gov/solar-activity/en/&quot;&gt;太陽黑子&lt;/a&gt;活躍區的附近。

這幅&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/DKdCCghIWwv/&quot;&gt;主題影像&lt;/a&gt;所示的四個位於&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/sun/&quot;&gt;太陽&lt;/a&gt;邊緣的日冕環，攝於2024至2025年間。

這些影像由位於&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy&quot;&gt;義大利&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/itj-85yLTK8&quot;&gt;曼托瓦&lt;/a&gt;的一部小望遠鏡，攝於&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/new-evidence-our-neighborhood-in-space-is-stuffed-with-hydrogen/&quot;&gt;氫原子&lt;/a&gt;發光的&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrogen-alpha&quot;&gt;氫α&lt;/a&gt;波段。

有時日珥會&lt;a href=&quot;https://styles.redditmedia.com/t5_2yb9w/styles/communityIcon_lqalsz65mlf51.jpg?format=pjpg&amp;amp;s=b08cef3aa70e534d3a5d8fbc180ad4844451779f&quot;&gt;突然斷裂&lt;/a&gt;，並將高能粒子&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap240818.html&quot;&gt;拋入&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/&quot;&gt;太陽系&lt;/a&gt;裡，造成一系列的&lt;a href=&quot;https://spaceplace.nasa.gov/spaceweather/&quot;&gt;太空天氣&lt;/a&gt;事件，進而可能影響地球的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap230122.html&quot;&gt;天空&lt;/a&gt;景觀與各種&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrington_Event#Telegraphs&quot;&gt;電網&lt;/a&gt;迴路。


</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250730.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250730.html</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>A Helix Nebula Deep Field</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/Helix_GC_1080.jpg&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;螺旋星雲的深場影像&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 影像提供與版權： &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/GeorgeChatzifrantzis&quot;&gt;George Chatzifrantzis&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Is the Helix Nebula looking at you? No, not in any biological sense, but it does look quite like an eye. The Helix Nebula is so named because it also appears that you are looking down the axis of a helix . In actuality, it is now understood to have a surprisingly complex geometry , including radial filaments and extended outer loops . The Helix Nebula ( aka NGC 7293) is one of brightest and closest examples of a planetary nebula , a gas cloud created at the end of the life of a Sun-like star. The remnant central stellar core, destined to become a white dwarf star , glows in light so energetic it causes the previously expelled gas to fluoresce . The featured picture , taken in red, green, and blue but highlighted by light emitted primarily by hydrogen was created from 12 hours of exposure through a personal telescope located in Greece . A close-up of the inner edge of the Helix Nebula shows complex gas knots the origin of which is still being researched . Portal Universe: Random APOD Generator
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 

螺旋星雲在看你嗎？ 沒這回事，至少不是任何生物學上的行為，不過它的確看來很像一隻眼睛。 

它之所以稱為&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helix_Nebula&quot;&gt;螺旋星雲&lt;/a&gt;，是因為它貌似一個我們順軸望進去的&lt;a href=&quot;http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Helix.html&quot;&gt;螺旋&lt;/a&gt;。

實際上，我們現在知道它具有出奇&lt;a href=&quot;https://chandra.harvard.edu/deadstar/helix.html&quot;&gt;複雜的幾何結構&lt;/a&gt;，包括輻條狀的雲氣絲及廣袤的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap230507.html&quot;&gt;外暈&lt;/a&gt;。

螺旋星雲（&lt;a href=&quot;https://grammarist.com/acronym/a-k-a-or-aka/&quot;&gt;亦稱&lt;/a&gt; NGC 7293）是離我們最近最明亮的&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planetary_nebula&quot;&gt;行星狀星雲&lt;/a&gt;之一，而這團行星狀星雲則是類太陽恆星在生命末期時，所產生的氣體&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KXNSYo8ZdoU&quot;&gt;雲&lt;/a&gt;。

星雲中心孑遺下來的、注定會成為&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap231224.html&quot;&gt;白矮星&lt;/a&gt;的恆星核，則輻射出非常&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/ems/10_ultravioletwaves&quot;&gt;高能量&lt;/a&gt;的光，激發先前拋出的氣體輻射出&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YvN8zFhWn04&quot;&gt;熒光&lt;/a&gt;。

這張攝於紅、綠、藍等波段但以&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.astronomyknowhow.com/hydrogen-alpha.htm&quot;&gt;氫&lt;/a&gt;輻射的紅光為主色的&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=729866973075216&amp;amp;set=a.149603584434894&quot;&gt;主題影像&lt;/a&gt;，建構自一部位於&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greece&quot;&gt;希臘&lt;/a&gt;後院的私人望遠鏡，所累積的12小時長曝光觀測數據。

針對螺旋星雲&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UwAKNMC2PeM&quot;&gt;內緣&lt;/a&gt;所進行的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap080413.html&quot;&gt;細部觀測&lt;/a&gt;顯示，該處有許多來源不明、仍&lt;a href=&quot;https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2020MNRAS.491..758A/abstract&quot;&gt;有待研究釐清&lt;/a&gt;的複雜雲氣結。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250729.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250729.html</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Collision at Asteroid Dimorphos</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/undefined&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;撞擊雙衛一&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 影片提供: &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asi.it/&quot;&gt;ASI&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nasa.gov/&quot;&gt;NASA&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href=&quot;https://dart.jhuapl.edu/&quot;&gt;Johns Hopkins APL&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nasa.gov/planetarydefense/dart/dart-news&quot;&gt;DART&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asi.it/en/planets-stars-universe/solar-system-and-beyond/liciacube/&quot;&gt;LICIACube&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&quot;https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/nmc/spacecraft/display.action?id=2021-110C&quot;&gt;LUKE&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.iop.org/&quot;&gt;IOP&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Why was this collision so strange? In 2022, to develop Earth-saving technology, NASA deliberately crashed the DART spacecraft into the asteroid moonlet Dimorphos. The hope was that this collision would alter the trajectory of Dimorphos around its parent asteroid Didymos and so demonstrate that similar collisions could, in theory, save the Earth from being hit by (other) hazardous asteroids. But analyses of new results show that the effects of the collision are different than expected -- and we are trying to understand why . Featured here is the time lapse video taken by the ejected LICIACube camera LUKE showing about 250 seconds of the expanding debris field of Dimorphos after the collision, with un-impacted Didymos passing in the foreground. In 2026, Europe&#39;s Hera mission will reach the asteroids and release three spacecraft to better study the matter.
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 

為什麼這例碰撞如此奇特？

在2022年，NASA為發展地球防禦技術，使用&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/darts-small-satellite-companion-takes-flight-ahead-of-impact/&quot;&gt;飛鏢(Double Asteroid Redirection Test, DART)&lt;/a&gt;探測器主動撞擊近地小行星中的衛星&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/asteroids/&quot;&gt;雙衛一 (Dimorphos)&lt;/a&gt;。

此任務的主要目標，是希望藉由撞擊改變&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimorphos&quot;&gt;雙衛一&lt;/a&gt;繞行母小行星&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/asteroids/didymos/&quot;&gt;雙生星 (Didymos)&lt;/a&gt;的軌道週期，進而驗證偏轉技術用於未來小行星撞擊防禦任務中的可行性。

然而，後續觀測與&lt;a href=&quot;https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/PSJ/addd1a&quot;&gt;資料分析&lt;/a&gt;顯示，撞擊所造成效應，與任務團隊原先的&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/iijreaGHS3c&quot;&gt;預期&lt;/a&gt;有&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dutch.com/cdn/shop/articles/shutterstock_1073296643_360x.jpg&quot;&gt;差異&lt;/a&gt;，顯示其背後涉及更為複雜的物質結構與碎屑動力學過程。

這部由撞擊前布署的輕型意大利小行星成像立方衛星（&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asi.it/en/planets-stars-universe/solar-system-and-beyond/liciacube/&quot;&gt;LICIACube&lt;/a&gt;）之&lt;a href=&quot;https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/nmc/spacecraft/display.action?id=2021-110C&quot;&gt;LUKE相機&lt;/a&gt;所拍攝的縮時影片，記錄了雙衛一被撞擊後約250秒內，&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap221005.html&quot;&gt;碎片團&lt;/a&gt;擴張的過程，並可見到未受撞擊的雙生星從影像的前景掠過。

於2026年，歐洲太空總署(ESA)的&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.esa.int/Space_Safety/Hera&quot;&gt;Hera&lt;/a&gt;任務將布署三枚探測器，仔細探索受到撞擊後的雙衛一，以確認小行星動能撞擊轉向技術的可行性，及探測雙生星系統，從而增進人類對小行星的了解。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250728.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250728.html</guid><pubDate>Sun, 27 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Lightning over the Volcano of Water</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/LightningVolcano_Montufar_960.jpg&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;水火山上空的閃電&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 影像提供: &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.flickr.com/people/m_acubens/&quot;&gt;Sergio Montúfar&lt;/a&gt;  
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.flickr.com/photos/m_acubens/&quot;&gt;Pinceladas Nocturnas&lt;/a&gt;)
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: 

Have you ever watched a lightning storm in awe? You&#39;re not alone. 
Details of what causes lightning are still being researched , but it is known that inside some clouds, internal updrafts cause collisions between ice and snow that slowly separate charges between cloud tops and bottoms 

The rapid electrical discharges that are lightning soon result. 

Lightning usually takes a jagged course, rapidly heating a thin column of air to about three times the surface temperature of the Sun 
.
 The resulting shock wave starts supersonically and decays into the loud sound known as thunder . On average, around the world, about 6,000 lightning bolts occur between clouds and the Earth every minute. Pictured in July 2019 in a two-image composite, lightning stems from communication antennas near the top of Volcán de Agua (Volcano of Water) in Guatemala . Sky Surprise: What picture did APOD feature on your birthday? (post 1995)
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt;  

你是否曾敬畏莫名的看著雷暴系統嗎？  

其實上，許多人都有過相同的感受。

雖然&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning&quot;&gt;閃電&lt;/a&gt;的詳細成因仍在&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/topics/atmosphere/lightning/history&quot;&gt;研究中&lt;/a&gt;，
但我們知道在某些雲層內部，上升氣流會導致冰晶和&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap240121.html&quot;&gt;雪粒&lt;/a&gt;互相碰撞
，進而在雲頂與雲底之間逐漸造成&lt;a href=&quot;https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19880001070&quot;&gt;電荷分離&lt;/a&gt;，最終產生&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap210104.html&quot;&gt;瞬間&lt;/a&gt;的放電現象，也就是我們熟悉的&lt;a href=&quot;https://ghrc.nsstc.nasa.gov/lightning/&quot;&gt;閃電&lt;/a&gt;。

&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sn65RFvJKnk&quot;&gt;閃電&lt;/a&gt;通常沿著鋸齒狀、曲折不規則的路徑迅速前進，並將通道內空氣&lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulgurite&quot;&gt;瞬間&lt;/a&gt;加熱至約為&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/sun/&quot;&gt;太陽&lt;/a&gt;表面三倍的高溫。
劇烈且急促的加熱所產生的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap240104.html&quot;&gt;震波&lt;/a&gt;自通道中驟然爆發，以&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap070819.html&quot;&gt;超音速&lt;/a&gt;穿過空氣，最終化作為&lt;a href=&quot;https://ih1.redbubble.net/image.4790337142.9753/flat,750x,075,f-pad,750x1000,f8f8f8.jpg&quot;&gt;轟然&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spinoff.nasa.gov/Spinoff2005/ch_5.html&quot;&gt;雷&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap100427.html&quot;&gt;鳴&lt;/a&gt;回盪天際。
據估計，全球平均每分鐘約有&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lightningmaps.org/?lang=en#m=oss;t=3;s=0;o=0;b=;ts=0;&quot;&gt;6,000次閃電&lt;/a&gt;在雲層與&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/earth/facts/&quot;&gt;地球&lt;/a&gt;之間發生。
這張&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z2zjDdS3NzQ&quot;&gt;主題影像&lt;/a&gt;疊合自2019年7月拍攝的二張相片，畫面中劃破夜空的閃電，則始於&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/SfPbWdmvZRU&quot;&gt;瓜地&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala&quot;&gt;馬拉&lt;/a&gt;的&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volc%C3%A1n_de_Agua&quot;&gt;水火山&lt;/a&gt;（Volcán de Agua）山頂附近的通訊天線。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250727.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250727.html</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Globular Cluster Omega Centauri</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/oc_ls_2025_1024.jpg&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;半人馬座的球狀奧米茄星團&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;影像提供 &amp;amp;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/lib/about_apod.html#srapply&quot;&gt;版權&lt;/a&gt;: &lt;/b&gt;

Data acquisition - SkyFlux Team,
Processing -
&lt;a href=&quot;https://app.astrobin.com/u/spinlock&quot;&gt;Leo Shatz&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Globular star cluster Omega Centauri packs about 10 million stars much older than the Sun into a volume some 150 light-years in diameter. Also known as NGC 5139, at a distance of 15,000 light-years it&#39;s the largest and brightest of 200 or so known globular clusters that roam the halo of our Milky Way galaxy. Though most star clusters consist of stars with the same age and composition, the enigmatic Omega Cen exhibits the presence of different stellar populations with a spread of ages and chemical abundances. In fact, Omega Cen may be the remnant core of a small galaxy merging with the Milky Way. With a yellowish hue , Omega Centauri&#39;s red giant stars are easy to pick out in this sharp telescopic view . A two-decade-long exploration of the dense star cluster with the Hubble Space Telescope has revealed evidence for a massive black hole near the center of Omega Centauri .
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 

在球狀的&lt;a href=&quot;https://earthsky.org/clusters-nebulae-galaxies/omega-centauri-milky-ways-prize-star-cluster&quot;&gt;半人馬座奧米茄星團&lt;/a&gt;裡頭，大約1千萬顆遠比太陽年老的恆星，擁擠在直徑約150光年的體積之內。 

亦名為NGC 5139、離我們約15,000光年遠的這個星團，是在我們銀河系銀暈內漫遊的200多個&lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Globular_clusters&quot;&gt;球狀星團&lt;/a&gt;中，最大與最明亮的一個。 

在大多數的星團裡，成員星具有相同的年齡和化學組成，然而謎樣的奧米茄星團卻有&lt;a href=&quot;https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2021A%26A...653L...8L/abstract&quot;&gt;不同&lt;/a&gt;分群的恆星，各自擁有不同的年齡層和化學組成。

因此，&lt;a href=&quot;https://esahubble.org/news/heic0809/&quot;&gt;奧米茄星團&lt;/a&gt;或許是一個小星系被我們的銀河吞併後，所&lt;a href=&quot;https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2019NatAs...3..667I/abstract&quot;&gt;孑遺&lt;/a&gt;下來的星系核。 

在這幅&lt;a href=&quot;https://app.astrobin.com/i/7na4mz&quot;&gt;清晰的望遠鏡彩色影像&lt;/a&gt;裡，奧米茄星團&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap151224.html&quot;&gt;泛黃&lt;/a&gt;的紅巨星輕易可辨。 

此外，使用哈伯太空望遠鏡對這個緻密星團進行了長達20年的探索之後，找到了&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/missions/hubble/nasas-hubble-finds-strong-evidence-for-intermediate-mass-black-hole-in-omega-centauri/&quot;&gt;奧米茄星團的中心&lt;/a&gt;附近有個大質量黑洞的證據。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250726.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250726.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Twelve Years of Kappa Cygnids</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/KCG2021_08_11_Pano_Elafonisi_met_fin-CCMZ_1024px.png&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;十二年的天鵝κ流星雨&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;影像提供 &amp;amp;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/lib/about_apod.html#srapply&quot;&gt;版權&lt;/a&gt;: &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.petrhoralek.com/#about-1&quot;&gt;Petr Horálek&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/josef.kujal/&quot;&gt;Josef Kujal&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href=&quot;https://tomasslovinsky.com/#about&quot;&gt;Tomáš Slovinský&lt;/a&gt;;
&lt;i&gt;Acknowledgement:&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://mahdizamani.com/&quot;&gt;Mahdi Zamani&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Meteors from the Kappa Cygnid meteor shower are captured in this time-lapse composite skyscape. The minor meteor shower, with a radiant not far from its eponymous star Kappa Cygni, peaks in mid-August, almost at the same time as the much better-known and better-observed Perseid meteor shower. But, seen to have a peak rate of only about 3 meteors per hour, Kappa Cygnids are vastly outnumbered by the more popular, prolific Perseid shower&#39;s meteors that emanate from the heroic constellation Perseus. To capture dozens of Kappa Cygnids, this long term astro-imaging project compiled meteors in exposures selected from over 51 August nights during the years 2012 through 2024. Most of the exposures with identified Kappa Cygnid meteors were made in August 2021, a high point of the shower&#39;s known 7-year activity cycle. All twelve years worth of Kappa Cygnids are registered against a base sea and night skyscape of the Milky Way above Elafonisi Beach, Crete, Greece, also recorded in August of 2021.
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 

這幅縮時的合成天空影像，呈現了來自&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kappa_Cygnids&quot;&gt;天鵝κ流星雨&lt;/a&gt;（Kappa Cygnid meteor shower）的流星。

這群小流星雨的&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiant_(meteor_shower)&quot;&gt;輻射點&lt;/a&gt;離據以得名的天鵝κ星（Kappa Cygni）不遠，而它在八月中旬的活動極大期，幾乎與更知名且更熱門的英仙流星雨同期。

不過，天鵝κ流星雨的峰值流星出現率僅有每小時3顆，遠遠少於&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap230809.html&quot;&gt;英仙流星雨&lt;/a&gt;的流星出現率。

也因此，為了累積數十顆天鵝κ流星，這項長期的天文攝影計畫，在2012年至2024年8月的51個夜晚進行觀測取像，才得以合成出這幅流星影像。

影像中，大多數&lt;a href=&quot;https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2025A%26A...695A..83B/abstract&quot;&gt;經過確認的天鵝κ流星&lt;/a&gt;記錄於2021年8月，而這也是這群流星雨已知的7年活動週期的高峰。

與這些&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.petrhoralek.com/?p=25643&quot;&gt;十二年天鵝κ流星&lt;/a&gt;疊合的希臘克里特島埃拉福尼西海灘海景及上方的夜空銀河，亦是攝於2021年的8月。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250725.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250725.html</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Titan Shadow Transit</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/SaturnJuly18_2025TitanShadowTransit1024.png&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;泰坦的影子凌土星&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt;影像提供與&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/lib/about_apod.html#srapply&quot;&gt;版權&lt;/a&gt;: &lt;/b&gt;

Volodymyr Andrienko

 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Every 15 years or so , Saturn&#39;s rings are tilted edge-on to our line of sight. As the bright, beautiful ring system grows narrower and fainter it becomes increasingly difficult to see for denizens of planet Earth . But it does provide the opportunity to watch transits of Saturn&#39;s moons and their dark shadows across the ringed gas giant&#39;s still bright disk. Of course Saturn&#39;s largest moon Titan is the easiest to spot in transit. In this telescopic snapshot from July 18, Titan itself is at the upper left, casting a round dark shadow on Saturn&#39;s banded cloudtops above the narrow rings. In fact Titan&#39;s transit season is in full swing now with shadow transits every 16 days corresponding to the moon&#39;s orbital period. Its final shadow transit will be on October 6, though Titan&#39;s pale disk will continue to cross in front of Saturn as seen from telescopes on planet Earth every 16 days through January 25, 2026.
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt;

&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap090319.html&quot;&gt;大約每隔15年&lt;/a&gt;，土星傾斜的環面會與地球的視線幾乎重疊。

當土星明亮壯麗的環系變得越來越纖薄暗淡時，對&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap241123.html&quot;&gt;地球&lt;/a&gt;的觀測者來說，土星環也會變得難以察覺。

不過，這也提供了觀賞土星的衛星及其影子凌越土星明亮盤面的機會。

其中，土星最大的衛星-&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/saturn/moons/titan/&quot;&gt;土衛六(Titan 泰坦)&lt;/a&gt;-無疑是最容易觀察到凌土的天體。


在這張攝於7月18日的望遠鏡主題影像裡，&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/webbs-titan-forecast-partly-cloudy-with-occasional-methane-showers/&quot;&gt;泰坦&lt;/a&gt;位於影像左上角，其圓形影子投射在土星條紋狀的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap170916.html&quot;&gt;雲頂&lt;/a&gt;之上，而纖薄的土星環亦清晰可見。


事實上，目前正值泰坦&lt;a href=&quot;https://skyandtelescope.org/astronomy-news/observing-news/titan-shadow-transit-season-underway/&quot;&gt;凌土星季&lt;/a&gt;的高峰，每隔16天便會上演一次影子凌土星的景觀，這與其繞行土星的軌道週期一致。

儘管這個凌土星季最後一次泰坦影子凌越將發生在10月6日，然而如用地面的望遠鏡觀測，泰坦暗淡的盤面仍會繼續以相同的週期掠過土星前方，直到2026年1月25日方止。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250724.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250724.html</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Fireball over Cape San Blas</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/MeteorMilkyWay_Rice_960.jpg&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;聖布拉斯角上空的火流星&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 影像提供與版權： &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/jriceastro/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Jason Rice&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Have you ever seen a fireball? In astronomy, a fireball is a very bright meteor -- one at least as bright as Venus and possibly brighter than even a full Moon . Fireball s are rare -- if you see one you are likely to remember it for your whole life. Physically, a fireball is a small rock that originated from an asteroid or comet that typically leaves a fading smoke trail of gas and dust as it shoots through the Earth&#39;s atmosphere . It is unlikely that any single large ground strike occurred -- much of the rock likely vaporized as it broke up into many small pieces. The featured picture was captured last week from a deadwood beach in Cape San Blas , Florida , USA . Piece it Back Together: Astronomy Puzzle of the Day
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 
你看過火流星嗎？

在天文學裡，&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.amsmeteors.org/fireballs/faqf/&quot;&gt;火流星&lt;/a&gt;是指非常明亮的&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/meteors-meteorites/&quot;&gt;流星&lt;/a&gt;，其亮度至少與&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap230306.html&quot;&gt;金星&lt;/a&gt;相當，有時甚至勝過滿&lt;a href=&quot;https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5415/&quot;&gt;月&lt;/a&gt;。

&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap230916.html&quot;&gt;火流星&lt;/a&gt;十分罕見，如果你有幸親眼目睹，可能會&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shutterstock.com/image-photo/close-scottish-fold-cat-head-600nw-1276621966.jpg&quot;&gt;終生難忘&lt;/a&gt;。

以其物理本質來說，&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap211012.html&quot;&gt;火流星&lt;/a&gt;是小岩塊，&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap231126.html&quot;&gt;起源&lt;/a&gt;於&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/asteroids/&quot;&gt;小行星&lt;/a&gt;或&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comet_nucleus&quot;&gt;彗星&lt;/a&gt;，通常在穿過&lt;a href=&quot;https://spaceplace.nasa.gov/atmosphere/&quot;&gt;地球大氣&lt;/a&gt;時，會留下逐漸消散的氣體和塵埃&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap190430.html&quot;&gt;流星跡&lt;/a&gt;。

不過，它不太可能發生大型地面撞擊，因為岩塊在碎裂時會很快汽化。

這幅&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/DLa5D4sxVag/&quot;&gt;主題影像&lt;/a&gt;是在上週&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/DLaPqFTRiAx/&quot;&gt;攝於&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/united-states/&quot;&gt;美國&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florida&quot;&gt;佛羅里達&lt;/a&gt;州&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LCQhTcFGiSE&quot;&gt;聖布拉斯角&lt;/a&gt;枯木散布的海灘。

</description><link>http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250723.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap250723.html</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Jul 2025 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>A Double Detonation Supernova</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/image/2507/DoubleSN_ESO_1080.jpg&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt; 
&lt;b&gt;雙響炮超新星&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 影像提供: &lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eso.org/&quot;&gt;ESO&lt;/a&gt;, 
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unsw.edu.au/hdr/priyam-das&quot;&gt;P. Das&lt;/a&gt; et al.; 
Background stars 
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nasa.gov/&quot;&gt;NASA&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/mission/hubble/&quot;&gt;Hubble&lt;/a&gt;): K. Noll et al.
 &lt;br&gt; 

&lt;!--
英文原文:Explanation: Can some supernovas explode twice? Yes, when the first explosion acts like a detonator for the second. This is a leading hypothesis for the cause of supernova remnant (SNR) 0509-67.5 . In this two-star system , gravity causes the larger and fluffier star to give up mass to a smaller and denser white dwarf companion. Eventually the white dwarf &#39;s near-surface temperature goes so high that it explodes, creating a shock wave that goes both out and in -- and so triggers a full Type Ia supernova near the center. Recent images of the SNR 0509-67.5 system, like the featured image from the Very Large Telescope in Chile , show two shells with radii and compositions consistent with the double detonation hypothesis . This system, SNR 0509-67.5 is also famous for two standing mysteries : why its bright supernova wasn&#39;t noted 400 years ago, and why no visible companion star remains.
--&gt;
&lt;b&gt; 說明： &lt;/b&gt; 
超新星能夠爆炸兩次嗎？

當然可以，由第一次爆炸充當&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detonator&quot;&gt;引信&lt;/a&gt;點燃了第二次更劇烈的大爆炸，就會出現這樣罕見的現象。

這是天文學家對超新星殘骸（Supernova remnant, SNR）&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eso.org/public/videos/eso2511b/&quot;&gt;0509-67.5&lt;/a&gt;，到底是如何形成的所提出的主要假說。

在這個&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap970219.html&quot;&gt;致密的雙星系統&lt;/a&gt;中，其中較大質量的膨脹恆星，會透過重力作用將質量&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roche_lobe&quot;&gt;轉移&lt;/a&gt;至一顆較小質量但密度更高的&lt;a href=&quot;https://science.nasa.gov/universe/stars/types/#white-dwarfs&quot;&gt;白矮星&lt;/a&gt;伴星。

最終，當&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap950910.html&quot;&gt;白矮星&lt;/a&gt;的表層物質不斷累積，導致其溫度升高到足以引發熱核爆炸，首次爆炸所產生的衝擊波&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eso.org/public/videos/eso2511c/&quot;&gt;同時向內外擴展&lt;/a&gt;，進一步在中心附近觸發第二次更劇烈的爆炸，形成完整的&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_Ia_supernova&quot;&gt;Ia型超新星&lt;/a&gt;。


最近來自&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eso.org/public/teles-instr/paranal-observatory/vlt/&quot;&gt;智利&lt;/a&gt;的&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eso.org/public/images/eso2511a/&quot;&gt;甚大望遠鏡(Very Large Telescope, VLT)&lt;/a&gt;所拍攝的&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eso.org/public/images/eso2511a/&quot;&gt;主題影像&lt;/a&gt;顯示，SNR 0509-67.5擁有兩層結構相似的殼層，其大小與成分都與所謂的「&lt;a href=&quot;https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2025NatAs.tmp..135D/abstract&quot;&gt;雙響炮&lt;/a&gt;」模型相符，進一步支持此假說。


除此之外，&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SNR_0509-67.5&quot;&gt;SNR 0509-67.5&lt;/a&gt;還伴隨著&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shutterstock.com/image-photo/funny-duo-two-black-white-600nw-1209024034.jpg&quot;&gt;兩個懸而未解的謎題&lt;/a&gt;：為何如此&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap110125.html&quot;&gt;明亮的超新星&lt;/a&gt;事件在約400年前，並未被人類所記錄？以及，原本的&lt;a href=&quot;http://sprite.phys.ncku.edu.tw/astrolab/mirrors/apod/ap120112.html&quot;&gt;伴星&lt;/a&gt;是如何消失得無影無蹤？


